## 4. Findings and Privacy Impact

| # | Technical Finding | Privacy Impact | Severity |
|---|---|---|:---:|
| 1 | Directory listing enabled on `/includes/`, `/assets/`, `/student/` | Exposes the exact filenames of scripts that handle student applications, certificates, profiles, and payments (`db.php`, `payu_config.php`, `certificate-payment.php`). Doesn't leak personal data directly, but reveals precisely where it lives on the server. | 🔴 High |
| 2 | Session cookie missing `HttpOnly` and `SameSite` attributes | Would make it easier for an attacker to hijack a logged-in student's session and access their personal data (applications, certificates, profile) if any script-injection issue existed elsewhere. | 🔴 High |
| 3 | No HTTP→HTTPS redirect enforced; HSTS not configured | Personal data (login credentials, form submissions) could be transmitted unencrypted if a user reaches the site over plain HTTP before any redirect occurs. | 🔴 High |
| 4 | Missing security headers (`CSP`, `X-Frame-Options`, `X-Content-Type-Options`, `Referrer-Policy`, `Permissions-Policy`) | Reduces browser-level protection against attacks (e.g. clickjacking, XSS) that could be used to manipulate a logged-in user into exposing their own data. | 🟠 Medium |
| 5 | No DNS CAA record; OCSP stapling not enabled | Minor certificate-issuance hardening gap; low direct impact on personal data. | 🟡 Low |

